  "title": "CHAPTER 1: HISTORY OF TAMIL NADU",
  "order": 1,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "ty27y1g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.1 Ancient Tamil History – Sangam Age"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Ancient Tamil history begins with the Sangam Age and its seminal literary works.",
        "The Pallava Dynasty (275 CE – 897 CE) and Imperial Cholas (850 CE – 1279 CE) shaped early and high medieval Tamil culture.",
        "Brihadeeswarar Temple stands as a major architectural landmark of the Imperial Chola era.",
        "Later medieval periods saw governance under the Pandyas, Vijayanagara Empire (1336–1646 CE), Nayaks, and Marathas in Thanjavur (1674–1855 CE).",
        "Colonial history spans European competition, Fort St. George, the Madras Presidency, and armed opposition during the Polygar Wars."
      ],
      "id": "n6roy7p"
    },
